<p>Paramount Skydance has agreed to acquire Warner Bros. Discovery in a deal valued at about $110 billion including debt—one of the biggest media consolidations in recent years. The offer prices Warner Bros. Discovery at $31 a share in cash, implying about $81 billion in equity value before adding the debt Paramount would take on. Together, the companies would combine major film and TV assets—Warner Bros., HBO, and CNN alongside Paramount’s businesses—into a larger global entertainment group as audiences continue shifting toward streaming. Netflix, which had been bidding for Warner Bros. Discovery, walked away after Warner’s board called the Paramount Skydance counteroffer “superior.” Netflix said matching that price was “no longer financially attractive”. The deal now moves into regulatory review in the United States and Europe, where some coverage flags possible antitrust scrutiny and questions about political influence, given David Ellison’s proximity to President Trump and Trump’s public demands for changes at CNN.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/xMlfCLL5UYbyc7KX_vbpZssRsmUCwpPwa8lbmdsdXULJHKDyYZQHoLvjqjrTisZMLI1Ofy0qjlDGKQJRZsTK6bxV_kYD7SL2n7tf5tJCRKt6XwR2LhF9VROUqomNU8cyroYuoE6MOs_YSY0Fi0HHXdK0FNjraN7DSXq2YiApIHR_zqWnfWqMr5FFc27ehGtBVK6uuPLj_90xvCtkQghQFd-1NI_tMkjUlnBG3op1ozk2e5miJCk0CvqbxSf6gDhyOkVWiNxJF7IQdw' alt='The Warner Bros. water tower at Warner Bros. Studios in Burbank, California, Feb. 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Match-right window: After Warner’s board called Paramount Skydance’s counteroffer “superior,” Netflix had four business days to match it—then chose not to.</li><li>How it was framed: The Associated Press called Netflix’s pullback a “stunning move,” effectively clearing the way for Paramount to take over a storied rival and its cable and news assets.</li><li>Specific flashpoint: A Paramount takeover would put CNN and CBS under David Ellison’s control, intensifying debate over how much sway one owner could have over major news brands.</li><li>Political proximity: Reporting noted that David Ellison and his father, Oracle billionaire Larry Ellison, are close to President Donald Trump, who has publicly demanded changes at CNN.</li><li>Size contrast: Commentary cited in coverage argued Netflix had the cash to raise its offer, while Paramount was described as “one-thirtieth” Netflix’s size—highlighting how unusual the bidding dynamics were.</li></ul><blockquote>This transaction was always a ‘nice to have’ at the right price, not a ‘must have’ at any price. - Ted Sarandos and Greg Peters</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Netflix leadership: Netflix portrayed its decision not to match as price discipline—saying the transaction was “no longer financially attractive” at the valuation implied by Paramount Skydance’s proposal, even though it had a contractual window to respond. (<a href='https://theweek.com/business/warner-bros-paramount-netflix-ellison-trump'>The Week</a>)</li><li>TD Cowen analysts: TD Cowen analysts wrote that approval from federal regulators “seems likely given the political environment,” while noting the deal still faces review. (<a href='https://theweek.com/business/warner-bros-paramount-netflix-ellison-trump'>The Week</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://theweek.com/business/warner-bros-paramount-netflix-ellison-trump'>Netflix drops Warner Bros bid, ceding to Paramount</a> - theweek.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/warner-bros-signs-us110-billion-deal-with-paramount/'>Warner Bros signs $US110 billion deal with Paramount</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/culture/article/2026/02/27/paramount-acquires-warner-bros-in-110-billion-deal-creating-hollywood-behemoth_6750945_30.html'>Paramount acquires Warner Bros. in $110 billion deal, creating Hollywood behemoth</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-discovery-unveil-megamerger/a-76159806'>Paramount and Warner Bros. Discovery unveil megamerger</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/warner-bros-signs-110-billion-deal-with-paramount-its-executive-discloses-in-townhall/article70685822.ece'>Paramount acquires Warner Bros. in $110 billion mega-merger</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>